  "cues": [
   [
    0.117,
    "Start with the thinnest fibre."
   ],
   [
    2.005,
    "Microfilaments are solid rods, about seven nanometers across."
   ],
   [
    6.562,
    "Each one is built from actin subunits, two strands of beads twisted around each other into a helix."
   ],
   [
    13.711,
    "Their main structural job is to bear tension, to resist pulling forces, a bit like the cables that hold up a tent."
   ],
   [
    21.159,
    "Just inside the plasma membrane, they form a three-dimensional network called the cortex, which helps support the cell's shape."
   ],
   [
    28.594,
    "And in intestinal cells, bundles of microfilaments form the core of microvilli, the tiny fingers that line the gut and soak up food."
   ]
  ]
 },
